      "writtenOn": "2024-08-27T22:32:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So this function stores into mMultiDraws, and then they get pulled out by `ExecuteICB`. I think this makes it a bit unclear how long mMultiDraws lives without closer investigation.\n\nI believe an alternative would be to have this function simply return the vector of multidraws, no member-variable stored.\n\nThe calling code could do something like:\n\n```\nstd::vector\u003c\u003e multidraws;\nDAWN_TRY_ASSIGN(multidraws, PrepareMultiDraws(...));\n```\n\nthen you pass multidraws into `this-\u003eEncodeComputePass`",
