      "writtenOn": "2024-08-28T06:01:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since we already have `if (cmdIndex \u003e\u003d drawCount)` I think we could use `dispatchThreadgroups` instead of `dispatchThreads`. IIUC the difference is basically that `dispatchThreads` will insert an `if (thread index \u003e\u003d number of threads)` check for you. It is probably a little more efficient than that, but it also only works on some hardware, so probably best to just avoid it (see the red box here: https://developer.apple.com/documentation/metal/mtlcomputecommandencoder/2866532-dispatchthreads?language\u003dobjc)",
      "revId": "ed816994106a23fa5404b0e6123e713079adfd96",
